    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0247" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">659.116Auto/4</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Owen</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 108</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-22">January 22, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Madam</hi>: I enclose copies, as listed, of recent
                    correspondence with Mr. Pyke Johnson, Vice President of the Automobile
                    Manufacturers Association, Washington, D. C.,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d139-f1"/> in
                    regard to the restriction of imports of American automobiles into Denmark.</p>
                <p>You are requested to do whatever you feel will be helpful in bringing about a
                    lessening of the import restrictions on American products.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis
                            B. Sayre</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
